  "notes": "E1, design situation A (sustained preparation). The opening builds Reactor Beta and Factories Beta and Gamma, so two reactors and three factories share the later work. From tick 1,200, four expeditions' equipment arrives on a fixed rhythm with no departure pressure: robot frames, then modules 300 ticks later, then bulkheads 300 ticks after that, delivered to the two Launch Pad holds alternately. Modules and bulkheads both take components, and bulkheads take a reactor's treatment, so pressing and treatment are shared work. Quantities are a quarter unit each, so two expeditions' equipment fits one pad hold (about 70%): nothing consumes it yet, and a full hold would stall the delivery and measure the hold rather than the policy. Equipment goes to a pad hold rather than Resource Storage, or one expedition's equipment would cover the next order without any work. Ticks are the engine clock, quantities milli-units.",
